Rehbrunn demonstration sites.

Rehbrunn is an invented German town. Every business in it is invented too.

index.html is the Vorlagensammlung. It presents the thirty sites as a template library
and serves as the town directory at the same time. Three views and five groupings and
thirteen pattern filters and a search browse the same thirty cards.

Each business has one folder holding a single index.html. The page carries its own style
block so no two sites share a stylesheet. That is deliberate because the set exists to
show thirty different designs.

Pages run from 223 to 385 lines. Among the navigation patterns are dropdown menus and
mega menus and tab panels and accordions and sticky sidebars and an off canvas menu and
a price calculator.

betriebe.md lists the businesses. Telephone numbers come from the range reserved for
fiction.

Scripts
-------
assets/vorlagen.py builds index.html. It reads every trader page and works out line
count and image slots and ground tone and typeface and navigation patterns. Run
`python3 assets/vorlagen.py` after changing a page. The trade data it starts from sits
in assets/betriebe.json.

assets/ecke.py puts the amber corner on every trader page. The corner marks the page as
a template and links back to the library. Running it again refreshes the corner in
place, so changing the wording or the size means editing the script and rerunning it.
The library page and the image worksheet carry no corner because neither is a template.

assets/aufnahmen.py takes a screenshot of every trader page and writes the preview
thumbnails the library cards use. Run `python3 assets/aufnahmen.py` after a page
changes, then rebuild the library. Two conditions apply because Firefox here is a snap
package. No other Firefox may be running, and the browser profile must sit in a visible
directory, so the script keeps it at ~/ff-aufnahme rather than under ~/.cache.

assets/bildnisse.py draws the portraits for named people. It uses DiceBear, which runs
locally and fetches nothing. The person's name is the seed, so the same name always gives
the same face. Install it once with `pip install dicebear-core dicebear-styles`. The
default style is open-peeps because it is CC0 and needs no credit line. `--stil personas`
switches style, and bildnisse.html compares twelve of them.

Facial hair is set per person in the LEUTE table rather than guessed from the name. A
random beard on a woman named in the page reads as a bug.

assets/bilder.py generates the placeholder images. Run `python3 assets/bilder.py` for
all thirty businesses or name one to redo a single set. `--bildnisse 4` adds four
numbered portraits for a team section.

Previews
--------
Each card in the library shows a real screenshot of the page behind it, captured at
1280 by 900 and stored at 800 pixels wide under assets/aufnahmen. The first eight load
eagerly so the top of the library is never blank.

Images
------
Each business gets a hero at 16 by 9 and a Tafel at 4 by 3 and a Bildnis in square. The
colour family comes from the trade. Motif and scale and angle and light come from the
slot so the images on one page differ from each other. A real photograph replaces the
file of the same name and the page needs no change.

bildvarianten.html compares four ways of adding images and shows the markup for each.
bildnisse.html compares twelve portrait styles with the same four names and states the
licence of each.

The Apotheke am Lindenplatz is the worked example. It carries the generated images and a
drawn mark and six drawn symbols and a drawn site plan.

Placeholder images carry an empty alt attribute because they show nothing. Real
photographs need a real description there.

Open index.html in a browser. There is no build step and nothing to install.
